REM ===== Experiment F: Trace element → real mass (super template validation) =====
REM Purpose: Validate the "super template" approach
REM Scenario: If the .equi was created with W at trace amount (1e-10),
REM           can SET REACTANT change it to a real value and get meaningful results?
REM This simulates what would happen with a super template where unused
REM elements start at 1e-10 and active ones get SET REACTANT to real values.
VARIABLE %EquiFile %OutDir
REM HIDE
REM HIDE_MACRO

%EquiFile = "D:\Nercar\Wuhu\Apps\factsage_app\inclusionprecipitation\demo\case.equi"
%OutDir   = "D:\Nercar\Wuhu\Apps\factsage_app\inclusionprecipitation\demo\test_output\testF\"

OPEN %EquiFile

REM Simulate "super template" usage:
REM   - W was originally 0.2g, set to 1e-10 (pretend it's "disabled")
REM   - Zr was originally 0.05g, set to 1e-10 (pretend it's "disabled")
REM   - B was originally 0.01g, set to 1e-10 (pretend it's "disabled")
REM   - Ti increased to 8.0g (user wants more Ti)
REM   - Adjust Fe to keep total ~100g
REM   Original total = 100g. Remove W(0.2) + Zr(0.05) + B(0.01) = 0.26g
REM   Add Ti delta = 8.0 - 5.4 = 2.6g
REM   Fe = 58.785 + 0.26 - 2.6 = 56.445g
SET REACTANT W MASS 1e-10
SET REACTANT Zr MASS 1e-10
REM Skip B for now — single letter conflicts with macro parser
REM SET REACTANT B MASS 1e-10
SET REACTANT Ti MASS 8.0
REM Fe = 58.785 + 0.2(W) + 0.05(Zr) - 2.6(Ti delta) = 56.435g
REM (keeping B at original 0.01g since we can't SET it)
SET REACTANT Fe MASS 56.435

CALC
SAVE "%OutDirEquiF.res"

END
